domain ADR0033:
  description "ADR-0033 revision 1: Runtime config is not durable run identity. Status Accepted."

problem P1:
  |
    Decide whether provider transport and worker execution Config revisions must be
    part of durable semantic-authoring run identity when recovery creates a new run.

evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted foundation requirements allow a failed attempt to terminate and an
    explicit retry to reconstruct a new attempt from source. Intermediate model or
    worker checkpoint persistence is not required.

evidence E2:
  |
    Accepted design revision five ends the current run after process or worker-lease
    loss and makes owner retry create a new run, but also proposes two additional
    durable configuration revision identity fields.

evidence E3:
  |
    Current WIP selects one provider transport configuration and one worker execution
    configuration at startup. The two proposed independent run columns do not exist.

evidence E4:
  |
    ADR0032 requires separate provider and worker time controls, fenced late-result
    rejection, and distinct technical outcomes. It does not require a later attempt to
    replay the expired run's worker configuration.

evidence OWNER_DIRECTION:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, after the distinction between nonpersistent worker state and a
    persisted configuration identity was explained, the product owner instructed that
    strict management be relaxed, the plan revised, and the next task proposed.

premise REQUIRED_DURABILITY:
  |
    Source and target identity, provider request lifecycle, reservations, receipts,
    monotonic accounting, fencing, questions and answers, technical outcomes, and final
    candidate metadata directly protect durable correctness.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Persist two configuration revision identities; persist complete configuration
    snapshots; or keep transport and worker values in startup runtime configuration
    while persisting only correctness-bearing facts.

pending U1:
  |
    No accepted compliance, billing, exact-replay, or service-level requirement has
    been identified that independently requires durable worker Config history.

evidence REVIEW_RESULT:
  |
    Formal review of exact ADR0033 revision one and conforming implementation-design
    revision six reports PASS with no P0 through P3 findings. The review reasoning
    SHA256 is cdd328284fd76310ef28dfaff0f59c2e7cf559828c738a3a71c85839be1567d3.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, immediately after the PASS result and complete Japanese review scope
    were presented, the product owner replied "ACCEPT". The reviewed pre-acceptance
    ADR SHA256 was ae8b736857b59188880acbf397e2da941caf5c102539b2410ddd7011fd1f529a,
    and the conforming implementation-design revision-six SHA256 was
    a0f2ba909d3c71fb7de2235bd84125b420663f6f8b5400c4236eaf92e832ebff.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, OWNER_DIRECTION, REQUIRED_DURABILITY, OPTIONS, U1:
  |
    Propose startup runtime configuration without transport or worker configuration
    revision identities or snapshots in SemanticAuthoringRunV1. Preserve every durable
    correctness-bearing fact named in REQUIRED_DURABILITY.

decision D2 based_on D1, E1, E4:
  |
    Same-run provider transport recovery may use immutable configuration held by the
    live execution. Process or worker-lease loss ends that run; explicit retry creates
    a new source-reconstructed run under the configuration active for the new execution.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, U1:
  |
    Permit bounded operational telemetry for diagnosis without making it a replay
    contract or semantic-correctness condition. Any future exact-replay or compliance
    requirement needs a separately accepted persistence decision.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on REVIEW_RESULT, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, D1, D2, D3:
  |
    Accept exact ADR0033 revision one and the conforming implementation-design revision
    six persistence direction. This acceptance does not select exact Config values or
    authorize implementation, commit, push, provider calls, deployment, migration,
    activation, rollback, or release.
